course: dictionary
lesson: 10544
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word umbrella is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «Put up your umbrella, it is pouring with rain.» Here an umbrella is a cover on a folding frame and stick that keeps you dry.
explain: «Sam sat under the beach umbrella all afternoon.» The beach and the sun tell you this is a sun umbrella, which keeps off the sun. The clues are the words around the word, so use them every time.
explain: An umbrella can also be a word for a group. A word that covers many smaller things together is called an umbrella term. «Dogs, cats and rabbits are all pets» is a sentence where pets is the umbrella term, because pets covers all of them.
fact: Umbrella is a noun. Its plural is umbrellas.
fact: An umbrella is a cover of cloth on a folding frame and stick that keeps you dry in the rain.
fact: A beach umbrella or sun umbrella keeps off the sun.
fact: An umbrella term or group covers many smaller things together.
fact: «Umbrellas» were known in ancient Egypt and Assyria, as sunshades.
exercise: «He put up his umbrella as the rain began.» What is an umbrella here? | A kind of hat | A strong gust of wind | A tall tree on the hill | *A cover on a frame that keeps you dry
exercise: «Sam sat under the beach umbrella all afternoon.» Why did Sam sit there? | To catch the rain | To look for shells in the sand | *To keep off the sun | To paint a picture of the sea
exercise: Mia says pets is an umbrella term. Which words does pets cover? | *Cat, dog and rabbit | Sun and rain | Bread and jam | Tail and whiskers
test: «Water, sand and snow reflect UV, so you can burn even under an umbrella.» What does this sentence warn you about? | *You can still get sunburn in the shade of an umbrella | Umbrellas stop all light, so you are always safe | Sand never reflects the sun | Snow is always warm
test: A superstition is a rule with no reason behind it that people keep anyway, such as «umbrellas indoors». Which of these is a superstition? | Umbrellas are made of cloth | Umbrellas have a folding frame | Rain falls from clouds | *Not opening an umbrella indoors
exam: «Kites were flown in China by the 5th century BC, and sunshades and umbrellas were also known in ancient Egypt and Assyria.» Which place knew about umbrellas in this sentence? | *Ancient Egypt | A kite shop in China | Modern Scotland | The Red Sea
